title: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings/TrustedPaths
caption: {{$:/language/TiddlyDesktop/Settings/TrustedPaths}}
tags: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings

A wiki can always read files inside its own folder. Anything elsewhere on disk has to be trusted first — either because you chose it in a save dialog, or because you allowed it when the wiki asked.

Trusting a ''folder'' lets that wiki read everything underneath it, so prefer trusting individual files where you can.

Revoking takes effect the next time the wiki asks for the file.

<$list filter="[all[tiddlers]prefix[$:/TiddlyDesktop/Config/trusted-paths/]each[wiki]sort[wiki]]" variable="grantTiddler" emptyMessage="//No wiki has been granted access to anything outside its own folder.//">
<$set name="thisWiki" value={{{ [<grantTiddler>get[wiki]] }}}>
<div class="td-trusted-wiki">
<div class="td-trusted-wiki-name"><$text text=<<thisWiki>>/></div>
<$list filter="[all[tiddlers]prefix[$:/TiddlyDesktop/Config/trusted-paths/]field:wiki<thisWiki>sort[trust-path]]" variable="entry">
<div class="td-trusted-entry">
<span class="td-trusted-kind"><$text text={{{ [<entry>get[trust-kind]] }}}/></span>
<code class="td-trusted-path"><$text text={{{ [<entry>get[trust-path]] }}}/></code>
<$button class="tc-btn-invisible td-button td-trusted-revoke" tooltip={{$:/language/TiddlyDesktop/TrustedPaths/RevokeTooltip}}>
<$action-deletetiddler $tiddler=<<entry>>/>
{{$:/language/TiddlyDesktop/TrustedPaths/Revoke}}
</$button>
</div>
</$list>
</div>
</$set>
</$list>
